+## Area coordinators
+
+When the work has at least three areas that each hold at least two tasks, the main session fixes the design and the
+split into areas, creates one worktree and branch per area, and starts one area coordinator per area from that
+worktree: `python3 <Source directory>/scripts/role_runner.py area-coordinator --assignment <file> --result <file>
+--add-dir <worktree>`. The coordinator splits its area into tasks, assigns them to implementation workers, verifies the
+area's checks, and returns its branch, the check evidence, and the open items. The main session integrates the branches
+and runs the checks across the areas. An area with one task gets no coordinator, and there is no fourth layer: only the
+main session starts a coordinator, a coordinator starts implementation workers only, and its workers start nothing.
+Its workers count under the request's run cap, retry cap, and parallel limit.
+
 ## Failure and recovery
 
 On failure, hold dependent tasks and preserve completed work. Diagnose and settle the correction in the main session.
